IMPORT prelude

-- Health Sciences Authority Act 2001 (Singapore) -- execution under seal (s 4(3)), constitution, terms and meetings of the
-- Authority (ss 5, 7, 9), the definitions of "health product" and "tobacco product" (s 11(5)), the acts needing the Minister's
-- approval (ss 12(b), (c), 22, 41), protection from personal liability (s 16), the financial year (s 18), and the three
-- provisions that reach the public: misuse of the Authority's symbol (s 38), secrecy (s 39) and composition (s 40).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HSAA2001.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amending Act annotated in the text is
-- Act 5 of 2018.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. It is an institutional Act: it creates the
-- Authority and gives it functions; the health-product, medicines and tobacco regimes it administers live in other Acts. SCOPED
-- to the rules with decision content. Not encoded: the list of functions in s 11(1) beyond the two definitions, the general
-- powers in s 12 other than those needing approval, committees and delegation (ss 13, 14), staff (s 15), funds, estimates, bank
-- accounts and investment (ss 19-25), the 2001 transfer of property, staff, pensions, contracts and proceedings (ss 30-36), and
-- the saving (s 42).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Sciences Authority Act 2001 -- the Authority`

§§ `4(3) -- instruments under seal`

-- s 4(3): "All instruments to which the common seal is affixed must be signed by any 2 members generally or specially authorised
-- by the Authority for the purpose or by one member and the Chief Executive."
GIVEN `authorised members signing` IS A NUMBER, `the Chief Executive signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sealed instrument is properly signed` IF
        `authorised members signing` >= 2
    OR  (`authorised members signing` >= 1 AND `the Chief Executive signed`)

§§ `5 -- constitution`

-- s 5(1): the Authority consists of "(a) a Chairperson; and (b) not less than 6 but not more than 10 other members, all of whom
-- must be appointed by the Minister". (2) The Minister may appoint the Chief Executive to be a member.
GIVEN `there is a Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `other members` IS A NUMBER, `all appointed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the membership complies with section 5` IF
        `there is a Chairperson`
    AND `other members` >= 6
    AND `other members` <= 10
    AND `all appointed by the Minister`

§§ `7 -- term of office and resignation`

-- s 7(1): a member (including the Chairperson) holds office "for such term not exceeding 3 years as the Minister specifies in the
-- appointment, and may be re-appointed".
GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term of appointment is permitted` IF
    `term in years` > 0 AND `term in years` <= 3

-- s 7(2): a member "may resign from his or her office at any time by giving at least one month's notice in writing to the
-- Minister". Notice is counted here in whole months.
GIVEN `notice in months` IS A NUMBER, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation notice is sufficient` IF
    `notice in months` >= 1 AND `in writing` AND `given to the Minister`

§§ `9 -- meetings`

-- s 9(1): "At all meetings of the Authority, 5 members form a quorum."
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` >= 5

-- s 9(4): questions are "decided by a majority of votes of the members present and voting". (5): the person presiding "has a
-- deliberative vote and, in the case of an equality of votes, he or she also has a casting vote". The votes counted below already
-- include the presiding member's deliberative vote. Treating a decision at an inquorate meeting as not carried is an inference
-- from s 9(1); the Act states no consequence.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
        `the meeting is quorate` `members present`
    AND (    `votes for` > `votes against`
         OR (`votes for` = `votes against` AND `casting vote for`))

§§ `11(5) -- health product and tobacco product`

-- s 11(5): "health product" means any substance, preparation or device that "(a) is represented for use by humans; (b) whether
-- because of its presentation or otherwise, is likely to be taken for use by humans; or (c) is included in a class ... ordinarily
-- intended for use by humans, solely or principally for a therapeutic, preventive, palliative, diagnostic or cosmetic purpose, or
-- any other purpose for the promotion or preservation of human health and wellbeing", including (d)-(l) (treating disease,
-- contraception, pregnancy tests, anaesthesia, disinfecting, and "cleansing, fragrancing, deodorising, beautifying ... the
-- complexion, skin, hair, nails or teeth"). The (d)-(l) purposes are folded into the two purpose flags below.
DECLARE Product
    HAS `is represented for use by humans` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is likely to be taken for use by humans` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is in a class ordinarily intended for humans` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is principally for a therapeutic, preventive, palliative or diagnostic purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is principally for a cosmetic purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is principally for promoting or preserving human health and wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the product` IS A Product
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the product is a health product` IF
        (    `the product`'s `is represented for use by humans`
         OR  `the product`'s `is likely to be taken for use by humans`
         OR  `the product`'s `is in a class ordinarily intended for humans`)
    AND (    `the product`'s `is principally for a therapeutic, preventive, palliative or diagnostic purpose`
         OR  `the product`'s `is principally for a cosmetic purpose`
         OR  `the product`'s `is principally for promoting or preserving human health and wellbeing`)

-- s 11(5): "tobacco product" means "any cigarette, cigar or any other form of tobacco which may be consumed through smoking,
-- chewing or otherwise". The words "or otherwise" leave the mode of consumption open; only the presence of tobacco matters here.
GIVEN `contains tobacco in some form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is a tobacco product` IF
    `contains tobacco in some form`

§§ `12, 22, 41 -- what needs the Minister`

-- s 12: "power to do anything" for its functions, and in particular may (a) enter contracts; (b) "with the approval of the
-- Minister, acquire and hold such movable or immovable property"; (c) "with the approval of the Minister, form or participate in
-- the formation of any company, partnership or joint venture"; (e) join an international body; (f) charge fees; (i) grant loans
-- to staff "for any purposes specifically approved by the Authority". s 22: raise loans "from the Government or, with the consent
-- of the Minister, from any other source". s 41: make regulations "with the approval of the Minister".
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `entering into a contract`
    `acquiring property`
    `forming a company or joint venture`
    `joining an international body`
    `charging fees for its services`
    `granting a loan to an employee`
    `borrowing from the Government`
    `borrowing from a bank`
    `making regulations`

GIVEN `the act` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's approval is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `acquiring property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `forming a company or joint venture` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `borrowing from a bank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making regulations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `16 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 16(1): "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Authority or
-- other person acting under the direction of the Authority for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the
-- execution or purported execution of this Act or any other written law."
GIVEN `is a member, officer, employee or person directed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in executing or purportedly executing a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a personal suit is barred` IF
        `is a member, officer, employee or person directed by the Authority`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `acted in executing or purportedly executing a written law`

-- s 16(2): where the Authority supplies information to the public, neither it nor its people "shall be liable for any loss or
-- damage ... by reason of any error or omission of whatever nature ... or however caused if made in good faith and in the
-- ordinary course of the discharge of the duties". Unlike (1), this protects the Authority itself.
GIVEN `the error was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is shielded from liability for the information error` IF
    `the error was made in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `18 -- financial year`

-- s 18: the financial year "begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year". A financial year is named
-- here by the calendar year in which it begins.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year beginning in` MEANS
    IF `month` >= 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` - 1

§§ `38 -- the Authority's symbol`

-- s 38(2): any person who uses a symbol or representation "identical with that of the Authority, or which so resembles the
-- Authority's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" is
-- guilty of an offence: fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
GIVEN `used a symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `identical to the Authority's` IS A BOOLEAN, `resembles it so as to deceive or confuse, or be likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol offence is committed` IF
        `used a symbol`
    AND (`identical to the Authority's` OR `resembles it so as to deceive or confuse, or be likely to`)

§§ `39 -- secrecy`

-- s 39(1): "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions or when
-- lawfully required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by any written law", a person who "is or has been" a
-- member, officer, employee or agent of the Authority or a member of a committee must not disclose information "relating to the
-- affairs of the Authority or of any other person" obtained in the performance of duties. (2): fine not exceeding $2,000 or
-- imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
DECLARE Disclosure
    HAS `by a present or former member, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
        `of information obtained in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN
        `for performing duties or functions` IS A BOOLEAN
        `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
        `required or allowed by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the secrecy offence is committed` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `by a present or former member, officer, employee, agent or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `of information obtained in performing duties`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `for performing duties or functions`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by a written law`)

§§ `38(2), 39(2) -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Authority's symbol`
    `breaching secrecy`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 12

§§ `40 -- composition`

-- s 40(1): "The Chief Executive or any officer authorised by the Chief Executive may compound any offence under this Act that is
-- prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum of money not exceeding $1,000." (2): on payment "no further
-- proceedings are to be taken". No offence is prescribed in the Act itself; prescription is left to regulations (s 41).
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `by the Chief Executive or an officer authorised by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is lawful` IF
        `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    AND `by the Chief Executive or an officer authorised by the Chief Executive`
    AND `sum collected` > 0
    AND `sum collected` <= 1000

GIVEN `the composition was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further proceedings are barred` IF
    `the composition was lawful` AND `the sum was paid`
